non July 25, 2024, by Executive Order 14125 of July 24, 2024 (Establishing \nan Emergency Board to Investigate a Dispute Between New Jersey Transit \nRail Operations and Its Locomotive Engineers Represented by the Brother-\nhood of Locomotive Engineers and Trainmen). That emergency board termi-\nnated upon submission of its report to the President. Subsequently, its \nrecommendations were not accepted by the parties. \nA party empowered by the RLA has requested that the President establish \na second emergency board pursuant to section 9A of the RLA (45 U.S.C. \n159a). \nSection 9A(e) of the RLA provides that the President, upon such request, \nshall appoint a second emergency board to investigate and report on the \ndispute. \nNOW, THEREFORE, by the authority vested in me as President by the \nConstitution and the laws of the United States, including section 9A of \nthe RLA","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-fr-originals-14128-df9fcb0e32.txt","sha256":"67850640d01ba453d12b2a7df8755fee4307963fc0f7322a704e64d010bfeb06","source":{"line":4440,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"aa700dc278ca2ffdd43d5dce0fe9aa8b82b11dce161dee273da82af60ee7f790"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:14128\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2024-11-26/pdf/2024-27850.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: df9fcb0e32552e0c74c22c14a28663be2858ceda80359af95ba6df17a91154d3\nLocation: 89 FR 93145, PDF pages 1-2 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 1 of 2 ===\nPresidential Documents\n93145 Federal Register / Vol. 89, No. 228 / Tuesday, November 26, 2024 / Presidential Documents \nExecutive Order 14128 of November 21, 2024 \nEstablishing a Second Emergency Board To Investigate a Dis-\npute Between New Jersey Transit Rail Operations and Its Lo-\ncomotive Engineers Represented by the Brotherhood of Loco-\nmotive Engineers and Trainmen \nA dispute exists between the New Jersey Transit Rail Operations and its \nLocomotive Engineers represented by the Brotherhood of Locomotive Engi-\nneers and Trainmen. \nThe dispute has not heretofore been adjusted under the provisions of the \nRailway Labor Act, as amended, 45 U.S.C. 151–188 (RLA). \nAn emergency board to investigate and report on the dispute was established \non July 25, 2024, by Executive Order 14125 of July 24, 2024 (Establishing \nan Emergency Board to Investigate a Dispute Between New Jersey Transit \nRail Operations and Its Locomotive Engineers Represented by the Brother-\nhood of Locomotive Engineers and Train","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_14128.txt","sha256":"a46027c27ff750ec1bd42701e135749c32a3bdac9747cd2d205c3576daed86b4","source":{"line":2338,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"9298a9b42752a625054c53b3f002ee9964faab8f0b9efd78b307aa97dee61d63"}}]}
